# Pairs with LogPrefixApplied. A call a predecessor on another silo abandoned,
# invisible to the shard's activation, lands beneath a later row of its own:
# readers pass it as a hole, then it appears beneath them. The base relies on
# each Azure Table provider instance committing phase 2 in offset order, so a
# predecessor's call lands only above every row that instance wrote.
MODULE: LogPrefixAppliedHiddenCallLandsOutOfOrder
TARGET: LogPrefixApplied
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a cross-silo predecessor's abandoned call lands beneath a later row of its own
PERTURBS: LateLand

--- FIND
               /\ occ[o] \in {"none", "ackedMid"}
               /\ \A p \in Offs : p > o => occ[p] \in {"none", "acked", "ackedMid", "late"}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the predecessor's instance commits phase 2 out of offset order.
               /\ occ[o] \in {"none", "ackedMid"}
--- END
--- FIND
WithCrossSiloMove == FALSE
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: raises the bound so a lost activation may move to another silo.
WithCrossSiloMove == TRUE
--- END
